id: pm-slack-3so4
title: Use the pm SDK mutation feed for Slack outbox recovery
description: "Adopt the canonical paginated mutation-event API for lifecycle recovery, preserve verified retained-history fallback and uncertain delivery semantics, and retain renderer defense in depth. Related SDK adoption: pm-slack-fitn."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: sdk-adoption
created_at: "2026-10-25T15:46:32.272Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T03:24:38.661Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-26T03:24:33.146Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T21:47:52.000Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Delivered by PR #158, merge e23ecfe839fbb85c55e47a1cd325abf153593d4d, merged 2026-10-25T21:47:52Z. index.ts uses SDK listMutationEvents pages only for candidate discovery, then authoritative readHistorySnapshot/locateItem/readLocatedItem and verifyHistoryEntries(history, currentDocument) before recovery. test/sdk-recovery.test.ts covers pagination, retained-history fallback, cache corruption, missing documents, mixed healthy/damaged neighbors and all-intents validation."
expected_result: "Canonical paginated recovery retains independent authoritative verification, healthy-neighbor progress and uncertain-delivery semantics."
actual_result: The focused recovery regressions pass on main; inspected recovery never treats cached events as integrity authority. A narrow SDK-mapped filename candidate inventory remains for unreadable inputs; upstream event-cache integrity and older digest coverage/review blockers are not claimed fixed.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-slack-fitn,related,"2026-10-25T15:52:27.938Z",codex-agent,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T15:47:15.676Z",codex-agent,"Plan: use listMutationEvents with full entries and opaque cursor pagination as the primary discovery path; preserve verified retained-history fallback when the event API cannot cover an old or malformed stream. Preserve lifecycle ordering, revision deduplication, eligibility snapshots and delivery uncertainty. Related SDK adoption item: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-slack-fitn.toon . Audit renderer finding requires no replacement: command-owned SDK renderers are already registered; local result-shape checks remain defense in depth. Dependencies stay pinned."
  "2026-10-25T15:52:30.067Z",codex-agent,"Replacement proof: reverted only captureSlackOutbox to origin/main while retaining the new tests and helper. node --test test/sdk-recovery.test.ts failed exactly one test: the canonical SDK feed projection was absent. The retained-history fallback test still passed. Restored the implementation. Full coverage: 476 tests passed; 100% lines, branches and functions across index.ts, outbox.ts and coalescing.ts. Renderer finding is already SDK-owned and deliberately retained, with no missing API."
  "2026-10-25T15:52:32.276Z",codex-agent,"Differential proof: freshly compiled origin/main 5c0bd37 versus candidate using read-only, non-git public tracker snapshots. pm-slack 5c0bd37: 700 inspected, 230 queued, 0 failed; pm-slack-standup f1d1187: 881 inspected, 237 queued, 0 failed. All 467 frozen payloads, revision receipts, eligibility contexts, repeated captures, item-filtered captures and ambiguous-destination holds matched exactly. Authoritative snapshot hashes were unchanged before and after; no git executable and no network sends. Zero intentional output differences. The SDK may create its disposable derived runtime projection."
  "2026-10-25T15:53:50.156Z",codex-agent,"Linked targeted test execution passed via pm test --run --progress. This tracker disables persisted test-result tracking, so the CLI returned a local receipt; results are recorded here without changing that policy. Full npm and Bun release gates will run with isolated HOME and git identity, matching clean CI discovery rather than optional host-global extensions."
  "2026-10-25T15:56:57.235Z",codex-agent,"SDK compatibility gap reproduced with real sealed history: listMutationEvents full entries normalize an RFC3339 +00:00 timestamp to Z, invalidating the original immutable record hash. Needed SDK capability: byte-faithful authoritative full history entries (or a projection that preserves the sealed entry timestamp). No upstream issue filed; orchestrator can report it. Package fallback now retries a projected stream from readHistoryEntries before declaring it invalid. The new offset regression failed before this fallback (0 inspected, 0 queued, 1 failed instead of 2/2/0) and passes after it. This preserves original behavior; no history is rewritten. Re-running final gates after the added regression."
  "2026-10-25T16:00:50.097Z",codex-agent,"Final validation after timestamp-compatibility fallback: linked typecheck, test typecheck, docstring gate and targeted tests passed (39 tests). Complete npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed with clean HOME and git identity: 477 tests each, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across all three shipped sources. Native Bun acceptance passed: one recovered lifecycle plus two coalesced events, two acknowledged HTTP sends, zero duplicates, no git. Re-ran the differential proof after the fix: all 467 public-corpus payloads/receipts remain identical and authoritative hashes unchanged. Final function-revert proof: two passes, one expected canonical-feed failure. Six original source lines removed; explicit SDK history fallback and already-owned renderers retained. No lint script is configured. Ready for review; owner verifies and closes the item."
  "2026-10-25T18:54:54.480Z",codex-agent,"Resumed after blocking read-only review. The cached mutation feed must be discovery-only: its self-consistent rows do not attest authoritative history. Plan: SDK readHistoryEntries plus verifyHistoryEntries on authoritative affected streams before replay, eligibility, deduplication or queuing; detect missing/truncated streams against retained feed evidence and authoritative item state. Add seeded corruption properties after index priming, both in-process and after process restart, with no git executable. Audit the entire PR for other cached-read substitutions. Preserve unrelated completed work and append-only tracker history."
  "2026-10-25T19:04:18.709Z",codex-agent,"Audit result: recovery is the sole direct-read substitution in this PR. Digest complete-list reads and SDK-owned renderers predate it. Mutation pages and the new complete-list inventory now supply candidate identities only. SDK authoritative history and current-item readers feed verifyHistoryEntries(history, currentDocument) before replay, eligibility, revision deduplication or enqueue. Each page candidate is verified or retained as a typed refusal before discovery cursor continuation; cursors are never persisted/acknowledged. Current-item candidates catch deleted/empty streams and current-document verification catches valid-prefix loss. SDK event pages have no authoritative integrity/completeness receipt; same-size corruption can leave cached rows self-consistent after restart. Orchestrator follow-up is needed; no upstream issue filed."
  "2026-10-25T19:04:51.193Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for blocking fix: kept all property tests and the authoritative reader, but restored only readOutboxMutationStreams and captureSlackOutbox from blocked head b84e769. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"primed SDK caches\" test/sdk-recovery.test.ts failed: 49 reported tests, 12 passed, 37 failed (including the parent). Same-size hash/byte edits were accepted with queued notifications and failed=0, including real process restarts. Twelve diagnostics showed source=derived_index and cached_chain_verifies=true despite damaged authoritative files. Restored the fixed functions. The initial fixed targeted run passed all 48 seeded corruption cases; final full coverage and gates include the CLI item-mismatch regression."
  "2026-10-25T19:06:58.318Z",codex-agent,"Verified-read validation: full coverage passed 527 tests, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across all three shipped source files. The corruption property passes all 48 cases (eight operators, three seeds, both in-process and fresh-process recovery), with zero inspected entries, zero queued intents and failed=1; filtered retries also refuse. Twelve same-size diagnostics show SDK source=derived_index and cached_chain_verifies=true despite corruption. The separate authoritative-item mismatch regression yields CLI exit 2 / history_unavailable. Linked typecheck, test typecheck, docstring and targeted tests passed via pm test --run --progress (89 tests). Healthy public-tracker differential rerun: 473 exact payload/receipt matches, zero output differences or authoritative-byte changes; snapshots recorded in docs/sdk-adoption-validation.md. Running final npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-25T19:13:24.362Z",codex-agent,"Final local release evidence for authoritative verification: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed 527 tests, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions over index.ts, outbox.ts and coalescing.ts. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstrings passed; no lint script is configured. Native Bun acceptance passed (one recovered lifecycle, two coalesced events, two acknowledged sends, zero duplicates, no git). All 48 corrupt-history cases and the typed authoritative-item mismatch test pass. Verification is unconditional on authoritative history/current-item bytes; cached pages/catalog rows supply only candidate identities. Revert proof, SDK missing-receipt gap and 473 exact healthy differential matches are recorded above and in the linked validation document. Releasing the claim for owner verification; item remains unclosed."
  "2026-10-25T19:17:13.258Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI exposed a Node 26 Bun-gate coverage gap: all 527 tests passed, but index.ts branch coverage was 99.77% (aggregate 99.82%) against the unchanged 100% threshold. Node 22 passed both release gates, and Node 26 npm/native Bun passed. Reproducing under local Node 26 to identify the missing deterministic scenario; no threshold changes and no CI retry in place of evidence."
  "2026-10-25T19:25:33.171Z",codex-agent,"Coverage follow-up: the original Node 26 full-suite reproduction passed 527 tests at 100%, so the CI branch miss was not deterministic. Extended the real legacy-history regression with a second item and an explicit item filter. Targeted Node 26 LCOV confirms the fallback-filter skip branch at index.ts:1985 now executes (0 hits before, 1 after), and the excluded item never queues. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstrings passed. Complete Node 26 bun run release:check now passes 527 tests with 100% lines/branches/functions across all three sources. No production code or coverage threshold changed in this follow-up. Original authoritative corruption properties and function-revert proof remain valid."
  "2026-10-25T19:30:31.593Z",codex-agent,"The new CI head passed both Node 26 release gates, but Node 22 npm reported the same single-branch shortfall with all 527 tests passing. Adding failure-only LCOV diagnostics to the coverage gate so CI identifies the actual zero-hit source range, while preserving its original status and the unchanged 100% thresholds. Reproducing the complete suite under local Node 22; no production recovery changes in this diagnostic follow-up."
  "2026-10-25T19:34:43.862Z",codex-agent,"CI acceptance: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40226450413 passed at dc3ba95. Both Node 22 and 26 jobs passed complete npm and Bun release gates: 527 tests per gate (2108 total), zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across all three shipped sources, and both native Bun acceptance runs passed. Local Node 22 coverage also passed 527 tests at 100%. Failure-only coverage diagnostics now print zero-hit LCOV source ranges without changing thresholds or failure status. All authoritative verification points, 48 seeded corruption cases, SDK cache-without-integrity-receipt gap and behavioral revert proof remain documented. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; no item closure, merge or release."
  "2026-10-25T19:41:57.189Z",codex-agent,"Failure diagnostics identified the actual incidental legacy branches: index.ts:2002 (historical identity/title validation) and index.ts:2013 (unknown-priority default). Added three real SDK-hashed historical snapshot cases with a restored valid current item. Identity/title cases report failure and publish no earlier buffered intent; the absent-priority case persists priority=4. All four reported tests (parent plus three cases) pass, together with typecheck, test typecheck and docstrings. This is a test-only coverage correction; authoritative recovery code is unchanged. Running the linked targeted suite and then exact-head CI again."
  "2026-10-25T19:43:49.943Z",codex-agent,"Final explicit legacy-field validation passed: linked typecheck, test typecheck, docstring and targeted suite reports 93 passing tests. Named Node 26 LCOV run hits all previously missing ranges at index.ts:2002 (5/2/4 hits) and :2013 (1 hit). The historical identity/title cases prove no earlier buffered intent escapes; missing priority persists as 4. All 48 seeded corruption cases remain in the linked suite. The full suite now contains 531 reported tests; final CI will enforce unchanged 100% thresholds for npm and Bun on Node 22 and 26. Implementation, authoritative verification points, healthy differential proof and behavioral revert proof are unchanged. Releasing the claim for orchestrator review."
  "2026-10-25T20:54:04.764Z",codex-agent,"Resumed for round-2 blockers. Replace strict whole-corpus inventory on recovery with fault-isolated identity discovery so one unreadable item cannot abort healthy recovery. Missing, empty, unreadable or malformed documents/history will each produce a typed per-item reason; no missing current document may reach the optional SDK verification parameter. Add mixed healthy/damaged multi-item properties with cache priming and actual restarts, plus separate behavioral reverts for both blockers. Reproduce stale event-cache behavior on SDK 2026.10.25 in a disposable project without changing the pinned SDK."
  "2026-10-25T21:23:03.756Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 design: current identity discovery reads filenames only, using resolveItemTypeRegistry and getItemPath for SDK-owned folders/formats. Missing pinned SDK API: an unreadable-inclusive identity/path iterator with typed per-row failures. SDK strict lists abort on a bad document; lenient candidate APIs omit it, so neither can certify all damaged candidates. Content, history parsing, timestamps and cryptographic/current-state verification still use SDK readers/isTimestampLiteral/verifyHistoryEntries. Missing current documents are explicit document_missing refusals; no undefined document reaches verification. Empty/missing/wrong-shaped histories and unreadable documents get typed per-item reasons in recovered.failures. All per-item intents are prevalidated through the shared outbox validator before the first write, preventing partial publication from a bad historical projection."
  "2026-10-25T21:23:06.722Z",codex-agent,"SDK current-release gap reproduced in an independent temporary project with exactly @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.25; repository pin/lock unchanged. Minimal steps: initialize a non-git tracker, create one item, prime listMutationEvents({full:true}), flip one record_hash hex byte in its history without changing byte length, then read full events in the same process and a fresh process. Both return source=derived_index with cached_chain_verifies=true while readHistoryEntries plus verifyHistoryEntries on authoritative bytes returns false. Page fields are count,cursor_mode,events,has_more,next_cursor,source: no integrity/completeness receipt. Reproducer: scripts/reproduce-sdk-event-cache.ts. No upstream issue filed."
  "2026-10-25T21:23:09.159Z",codex-agent,"Separate behavioral revert proofs: (1) replace only readOutboxItemIds with the blocked strict whole-corpus inventory, retaining all guards and tests: the mixed property fails all 6 cases (7 reported failures including parent), aborting recovery on damaged documents. (2) replace only readVerifiedOutboxHistory with blocked head 396cfb5 and its required SDK import: all 6 mixed cases fail (7 reported failures), queuing 13 instead of 10 intents because missing current documents and valid-prefix histories bypass comparison. Restored both fixes. Proof commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"mixed damaged\" test/sdk-recovery.test.ts. The existing round-1 cache-verification proof remains valid."
  "2026-10-25T21:30:03.052Z",codex-agent,"Third isolation revert proof: removed only the all-intents prevalidation step from captureSlackOutbox, leaving enqueue validation and other guards intact. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"invalid historical values\" test/sdk-recovery.test.ts fails on the historical negative delivery timestamp: enqueue throws invalid_input after an earlier intent was publishable instead of isolating the item. Restoring the prevalidation step passes all four tests. Shared validation is extracted once and reused; operational SQLite failures remain storage refusals."
  "2026-10-25T21:30:05.627Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 validation: full coverage passed 552 tests, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across all three shipped sources. Linked static/targeted suite via pm test --run --progress --timeout 240 passed 114 tests. Mixed property passes six 17-item runs (three seeds, both process modes): 72 damaged item instances are all reported with reasons; all 60 healthy create/block intents recover exactly once; repeated captures queue zero. Both review cases are included. Wrong-shape history fields, missing whole history directory, malformed historical projections and discovery-directory faults also isolate healthy neighbors. Fresh public tracker differential still matches all 473 payloads/receipts with unchanged authoritative hashes. Preparing final npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-25T21:35:51.850Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 local gates passed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 552 tests with zero failures/skips and 100% lines/branches/functions across all three shipped sources. Native Bun outbox acceptance passed with zero duplicates and no git. Linked targeted/static suite passed 114 tests. All mixed healthy/damaged cases, required-input guards, complete safe failure receipts and per-item publication validation passed. Both review-case reverts fail independently; removing publication prevalidation also fails. SDK stale-event gap still reproduces on exactly 2026.10.25 in a separate install; pin/lock unchanged. Healthy differential remains 473 exact matches. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; item remains unclosed."
  "2026-10-26T03:17:08.914Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit on main e23ecfe839fbb85c55e47a1cd325abf153593d4d: merged PR #158 (e23ecfe839fbb85c55e47a1cd325abf153593d4d, merged 2026-10-25T21:47:52Z). index.ts uses SDK listMutationEvents pages only for candidate discovery, then authoritative readHistorySnapshot/locateItem/readLocatedItem and verifyHistoryEntries(history, currentDocument) before recovery. test/sdk-recovery.test.ts covers pagination, retained-history fallback, cache corruption, missing documents, mixed healthy/damaged neighbors and all-intents validation. All scoped acceptance criteria are represented by the inspected implementation and regressions. Existing behavioural revert evidence is retained; this tracker-only audit changes no runtime functions."
